  "notes": "Four co-contributing failure modes (weld quality, nozzle loads, joint detail, vibration) each independently LEADS_TO the fatigue/cracking failure mode per rule 5's parallel-trigger guidance; only the design/fabrication-oriented origin (fm_weldquality) carries the CAUSED_BY edge to the Cause node since cause_code B (design/fabrication) governs category per rule 4, though narrative blends design and vibration factors. MSR FCV failure and N-35 instrument issue are secondary anomalies during the shutdown, included as components/systems (INVOLVES) but not merged into the main leak causal chain since narrative does not causally link them to the weld failure. Block 13 component field was blank/illegible in source; system code CB (seal injection) and manufacturer PSX (Westinghouse) retained per form. Similar-event LERs: text says '\"G\" RCP' for 2016 event but body abstract only references Unit 2 seal leak generically; kept as stated in narrative including apparent 'G' RCP designation possibly OCR artifact of 'C' RCP — recorded title verbatim per narrative wording where legible; LER numbers exactly as stated (2016-001, 1994-005) per rule 9, unit digit prefixed as '2-' since Unit 2 is the affected unit in narrative."
